    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d306-a2">

                <pb facs="0795" n="1425" xml:id="pg1425"/>

                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Vienna</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1868-12-21"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 21,
                        1868</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: With reference to my dispatch to Lord
                    Stanley, of the 8th instant, informing his lordship, in reply to the queries
                    addressed to me in his dispatch No. 70, circular of the 11th of August, that
                    according to the law of the western (Cisleithan) portion of the empire all
                    children horn of foreign parents in Austria are regarded as aliens, illegitimate
                    children of aliens being regarded to follow the nationality of the mother, I
                    have now the honor to inclose to your lordship a translation of a note I have
                    this day received from the imperial chancery of State, stating that the laws of
                    Hungary on that point are identical with those of Cisleitha.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>A. G. G. BONAR.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl of Clarendon</hi>, K. G., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
